    {
      "id": "a1-03-l3",
      "title": "Non lavoro. Dove abiti?",
      "minutes": 8,
      "goal": "You can say what you don't do and ask simple questions.",
      "takeaway": "Put non before the verb. Ask with dove, che cosa… and the verb.",
      "exercises": [
        {
          "type": "translate",
          "id": "a1-03-l3-e01",
          "stage": "warmup",
          "instruction": "Traduci.",
          "direction": "it_en",
          "source": "Abito a Roma.",
          "answers": [
            "I live in Rome.",
            "I live in Rome"
          ],
          "explanation": "Abito is the io form of abitare."
        },
        {
          "type": "grammar_note",
          "id": "a1-03-l3-e02",
          "stage": "learn",
          "title": "Non",
          "body": "Put **non** before the verb to make a negative.\n\n| sì | no |\n|---|---|\n| Parlo francese. | ==Non== parlo francese. |\n| Abito a Roma. | ==Non== abito a Roma. |\n| Studiamo. | ==Non== studiamo. |\n\n> Italian does not need a helper like English *do*: **Non parlo** = I do not speak.",
          "examples": [
            {
              "it": "Non parlo francese.",
              "en": "I don't speak French."
            },
            {
              "it": "Marco non lavora oggi.",
              "en": "Marco isn't working today."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "grammar_note",
          "id": "a1-03-l3-e03",
          "stage": "learn",
          "title": "Dove? Che cosa?",
          "body": "A question has the same words as a statement, with a question word in front.\n\n| domanda | risposta |\n|---|---|\n| ==Dove== abiti? | Abito a Torino. |\n| ==Dove== lavori? | Lavoro a Milano. |\n| ==Che cosa== studi? | Studio inglese. |\n\n> A yes / no question: just raise your voice. *Parli italiano?*",
          "examples": [
            {
              "it": "Dove lavori? Lavoro a Milano.",
              "en": "Where do you work? I work in Milan."
            },
            {
              "it": "Parli italiano?",
              "en": "Do you speak Italian?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "find_trigger",
          "id": "a1-03-l3-e04",
          "stage": "practise",
          "instruction": "Tocca la parola giusta.",
          "sentence": "Marco non abita a Milano.",
          "trigger": "non",
          "explanation": "Non goes right before the verb to make it negative."
        },
        {
